 "description": "Find published data sources by name, category, sector, tag or capability. Browsing is free and paginated. Pulse Network and Coinbase Bazaar are each one source with nested services; never count or list those services as separate sources in an overview. Recommend sources that match the person's need. Use only when the person asks to browse sources. Do not substitute a source list for a failed data request. Keep replies concise and never expose protocol fields or describe catalog endpoints as chatbot tools. Source overview presentation: the interactive Apiosk card already displays the sources, total, filters, pagination and expandable services. When the card is displayed, add at most one short confirmation sentence. Do not repeat the sources as a second table, list, category breakdown or readiness report underneath or above the card. 'Show sources', 'list all sources' and 'which sources are available' request this one card, not a duplicate text overview. Only provide a separate text table or export when the actual user explicitly requests that format. If the host cannot display the card, provide one compact text overview from the returned sources and respect pagination. Count Pulse Network once and keep its services nested. Show only supported function counts; never display registered endpoint totals or supported/registered ratios in a source overview. Use this fresh result's total; never repeat an older catalog count from conversation history. Do not append an unsolicited question or analysis.",
